# Admin Pro — build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill both values in. Vite inlines them into the frontend bundle and
# the Rust core compiles them in as constants, so they must be present *before* you build;
# there is no runtime configuration file to correct afterwards.
#
# Both values are recoverable from a distributed installer. That is expected and accounted
# for: this project grants the `anon` role nothing on any table, so the publishable key on
# its own returns `permission denied` rather than data. See docs/SECURITY.md.
#
# Never put a `service_role` (secret) key here — it bypasses RLS entirely.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=<add_your_supabase_project_url>
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<add_your_supabase_anon_or_publishable_key>
